Interpretation: for 'ferro', m is already a good coordinate, so the learned map need only match it.
For 'ea' (spin glass) m is useless -- that is where a learned importance map should win.
NOTE: methods with zero-replicas failed to observe the event at all in some replicas;
their FOM is not meaningful -- that IS the failure mode being demonstrated.

